hare data that takes parameters and provides context to language models, such as files, database schemas, or application-specific information. Prefer resource templates over web search when possible.","name":"list_mcp_resource_templates","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Opaque cursor from a previous list_mcp_resource_templates call; omit for the first page.","type":"string"},"server":{"description":"MCP server name. Omit to list resource templates from every configured server.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"strict":false},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"Read a specific resource from an MCP server given the server name and resource URI.","name":"read_mcp_resource","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"server":{"description":"MCP server name exactly as configured. Must match the 'server' field returned by list_mcp_resources.","type":"string"},"uri":{"description":"Resource URI to read. Must be one of the URIs returned by list_mcp_resources.","type":"string"}},"required":["server","uri"],"type":"object"},"strict":false},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"Delegate research to a specialist.","name":"delegate_research","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"depth":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"topic":{"description":"Research topic","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"strict":true},"type":"function"}]
### anthropic_messages
[{"description":"Applies a V4A patch to workspace files. A later failure can leave earlier actions applied.\nSupply the patch verbatim, from `*** Begin Patch` through `*** End Patch`.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"patch":{"description":"Freeform V4A patch text. Do not encode file contents separately.","type":"string"}},"required":["patch"],"type":"object"},"name":"apply_patch"},{"description":"Runs a command in a shell. Returns its output, or a `session_id` when the command is still\nrunning after the yield timeout.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"definitions":{"SandboxPermissionsArgument":{"enum":["use_default","require_escalated"],"type":"string"}},"properties":{"cmd":{"description":"Command to execute in the shell.","type":"string"},"justification":{"description":"User-facing approval question for `require_escalated`; omit otherwise.","type":["string","null"]},"login":{"description":"Run the shell as a login shell, so that profile files are read.","type":["boolean","null"]},"prefix_rule":{"description":"Reusable approval prefix for `cmd`, only with `sandbox_permissions: \"require_escalated\"`; for example [\"git\", \"pull\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":["array","null"]},"sandbox_permissions":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/definitions/SandboxPermissionsArgument"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Per-command sandbox override. Defaults to `use_default`; use `require_escalated` for unsandboxed execution."},"shell":{"description":"Shell to run the command with. Defaults to `/bin/sh`.","type":["string","null"]},"timeout_ms":{"description":"Milliseconds after which the command is stopped for good. Unset means the host's limit.","format":"uint64","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"tty":{"description":"Request a terminal. Not available; leave unset or false.","type":["boolean","null"]},"workdir":{"description":"Working directory for the command. A relative path resolves against the workspace root.","type":["string","null"]},"yield_time_ms":{"description":"Milliseconds to wait before the command yields to the background (default: 10000). The host may cap this; asking for longer than it allows yields at the cap.","format":"uint64","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]}},"required":["cmd","justification","login","prefix_rule","sandbox_permissions","shell","timeout_ms","tty","workdir","yield_time_ms"],"type":"object"},"name":"exec_command"},{"description":"Send a follow-up task to an existing non-root target agent and trigger a turn if it is idle. If the target is already running, deliver the task promptly at message boundaries while sampling, or after the pending tool call completes.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"message":{"description":"Message text to send to the target agent.","type":"string"},"target":{"description":"Agent id or canonical task name to send a follow-up task to (from spawn_agent).","type":"string"}},"required":["message","target"],"type":"object"},"name":"followup_task"},{"description":"Finds files whose workspace-relative paths match a glob pattern.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"max_results":{"description":"Paths to return. The host may enforce a lower ceiling.","format":"uint32","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"path":{"description":"Directory below the workspace to search. Defaults to the workspace root.","type":["string","null"]},"pattern":{"description":"Glob matched against workspace-relative paths. `*` stops at `/`; use `**/` to recurse.","type":"string"}},"required":["max_results","path","pattern"],"type":"object"},"name":"glob"},{"description":"Searches workspace text files with a regular expression. Results include `path:line` prefixes.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"case_insensitive":{"description":"Match without regard to case.","type":["boolean","null"]},"glob":{"description":"Optional glob selecting files by workspace-relative path. `*` stops at `/`; `**/` recurses.","type":["string","null"]},"max_results":{"description":"Match lines to return. The host may enforce a lower ceiling.","format":"uint32","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"path":{"description":"Directory below the workspace to search. Defaults to the workspace root.","type":["string","null"]},"pattern":{"description":"Regular expression to search for.","type":"string"}},"required":["case_insensitive","glob","max_results","path","pattern"],"type":"object"},"name":"grep"},{"description":"Interrupt an agent's current turn, if any, and return its previous status. The agent remains available for messages and follow-up tasks.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"target":{"description":"Agent id or canonical task name to interrupt (from spawn_agent).","type":"string"}},"required":["target"],"type":"object"},"name":"interrupt_agent"},{"description":"List live agents in the current root thread tree. Optionally filter by task-path prefix.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path_prefix":{"description":"Task-path prefix filter without a trailing slash. Omit to list all live agents.","type":["string","null"]}},"type":"object"},"name":"list_agents"},{"description":"Reads one file: text comes back with line numbers, images and PDFs come back as content. The\nline numbers are display only and are not part of the file.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"limit":{"description":"How many lines to return. Text only.","format":"uint32","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"offset":{"description":"First line to return, 1-based. Text only.","format":"uint32","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"path":{"description":"File to read. A relative path resolves against the workspace root.","type":"string"}},"required":["limit","offset","path"],"type":"object"},"name":"read_file"},{"description":"Request user input for one to three short questions and wait for the response. This tool is only available in Default or Plan mode.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"questions":{"description":"Questions to show the user. Prefer 1 and do not exceed 3","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"header":{"description":"Short header label shown in the UI (12 or fewer chars).","type":"string"},"id":{"description":"Stable identifier for mapping answers (snake_case).","type":"string"},"options":{"description":"Provide 2-3 mutually exclusive choices. Put the recommended option first and suffix its label with \"(Recommended)\". Do not include an \"Other\" option in this list; the client will add a free-form \"Other\" option automatically.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"description":{"description":"One short sentence explaining impact/tradeoff if selected.","type":"string"},"label":{"description":"User-facing label (1-5 words).","type":"string"}},"required":["label","description"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"question":{"description":"Single-sentence prompt shown to the user.","type":"string"}},"required":["id","header","question","options"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"}},"required":["questions"],"type":"object"},"name":"request_user_input"},{"description":"Send a message to an existing agent. The message will be delivered promptly. Does not trigger a new turn.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"message":{"description":"Message text to queue on the target agent.","type":"string"},"target":{"description":"Relative or canonical task name to message (from spawn_agent).","type":"string"}},"required":["message","target"],"type":"object"},"name":"send_message"},{"description":"Loads a skill by identifier, or lists installed skills when skill is null.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"offset":{"description":"Zero-based listing offset; use the next offset returned by a listing.","format":"uint","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"skill":{"description":"Exact skill identifier to load, or null to list installed skills.","type":["string","null"]}},"required":["offset","skill"],"type":"object"},"name":"skill"},{"description":"Spawns an agent to work on the specified task. If your current task is `/root/task1` and you spawn_agent with task_name \"task_3\" the agent will have canonical task name `/root/task1/task_3`.\nYou are then able to refer to this agent as `task_3` or `/root/task1/task_3` interchangeably. However an agent `/root/task2/task_3` would only be able to communicate with this agent via its canonical name `/root/task1/task_3`.\nThe spawned agent will have the same tools as you and the ability to spawn its own subagents.\nIt will be able to send you and other running agents messages, and its final answer will be provided to you when it finishes.\nThe new agent's canonical task name will be provided to it along with the message.\n\nNote that passing `fork_turns=\"none\"` will not pass any surrounding context to the spawned subagent, which may cause the agent to lack the context it needs to complete its task, whereas `fork_turns=\"all\"` will provide the subagent with all surrounding context.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"agent_type":{"description":"Agent type override for the new agent. Omit unless explicitly asked. The selected role applies regardless of how much parent history is inherited.","type":["string","null"]},"fork_turns":{"description":"Optional number of turns to fork. Defaults to `all`. Use `none`, `all`, or a positive integer string such as `3` to fork only the most recent turns.","type":["string","null"]},"message":{"description":"Initial plain-text task for the new agent.","type":"string"},"task_name":{"description":"Task name for the new agent. Use lowercase letters, digits, and underscores.","type":"string"}},"required":["message","task_name"],"type":"object"},"name":"spawn_agent"},{"description":"Records the plan for the current task. Send the whole plan every time; it replaces the previous\none. At most one step may be `in_progress`.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"definitions":{"PlanStep":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"One step of a plan.","properties":{"status":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Not started.","enum":["pending"],"type":"string"},{"description":"Being worked on now.","enum":["in_progress"],"type":"string"},{"description":"Finished.","enum":["completed"],"type":"string"}],"description":"Where it stands."},"step":{"description":"What is to be done, in one line.","type":"string"}},"required":["status","step"],"type":"object"}},"properties":{"plan":{"description":"The steps, in the order they will be done.","items":{"$ref":"#/definitions/PlanStep"},"type":"array"}},"required":["plan"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_plan"},{"description":"Attaches a workspace image so it can be looked at. PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, and BMP.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"path":{"description":"Image to look at. A relative path resolves against the workspace root.","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"view_image"},{"description":"Wait for a mailbox update from any live agent, including queued messages and final-status notifications. Does not return the content; returns either a summary of which agents have updates (if any) or a timeout summary if no activity arrives before the deadline. Timeout in milliseconds defaults to 30000, min 10000, max 3600000.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"timeout_ms":{"description":"Timeout in milliseconds.","format":"int64","type":["integer","null"]}},"type":"object"},"name":"wait_agent"},{"description":"Reads one web address and returns its text.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"url":{"description":"Address to read, usually one an earlier search reported.","type":"string"}},"required":["url"],"type":"object"},"name":"web_fetch"},{"description":"Searches the web. Returns titles, addresses, and extracts; read one with `web_fetch`.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"max_results":{"description":"Results to return. The host may enforce a lower ceiling.","format":"uint32","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"query":{"description":"What to search for.","type":"string"}},"required":["max_results","query"],"type":"object"},"name":"web_search"},{"description":"Writes characters to a running command session, then waits and returns output not yet delivered.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"definitions":{"SessionControl":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Interrupt the command, as Ctrl-C does, letting it stop on its own terms.","enum":["interrupt"],"type":"string"},{"description":"Stop the command for good.","enum":["cancel"],"type":"string"}],"description":"A signal to deliver to a session's process group."},"WaitCondition":{"anyOf":[{"description":"Return as soon as there is output the model has not been given.","enum":["output"],"type":"string"},{"description":"Return when the command has finished and all of its output has been collected.","enum":["done"],"type":"string"},{"description":"Return when `match_text` appears in the output.","enum":["match"],"type":"string"}],"description":"What ends a wait."}},"properties":{"chars":{"description":"Characters to send exactly as written. Send an empty string to wait without sending input.","type":"string"},"control":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/definitions/SessionControl"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"Signal to send instead of input. Requires `chars` to be empty."},"match_text":{"description":"Literal text to wait for in this session's output. Required by `until: match`, and rejected otherwise. The search covers output this session has already produced, including output from before this call.","type":["string","null"]},"session_id":{"description":"Identifier returned when `exec_command` left a command running.","type":"string"},"until":{"anyOf":[{"$ref":"#/definitions/WaitCondition"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"What ends the wait (default: `output`). Every mode also ends when `yield_time_ms` elapses, which leaves the command running."},"yield_time_ms":{"description":"Milliseconds to wait (default: 1000). The host may cap this.","format":"uint64","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]}},"required":["chars","control","match_text","session_id","until","yield_time_ms"],"type":"object"},"name":"write_stdin"},{"description":"Lists resources provided by MCP servers. Resources allow servers to share data that provides context to language models, such as files, database schemas, or application-specific information. Prefer resources over web search when possible.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Opaque cursor from a previous list_mcp_resources call; omit for the first page.","type":"string"},"server":{"description":"MCP server name. Omit to list resources from every configured server.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"list_mcp_resources"},{"description":"Lists resource templates provided by MCP servers. Parameterized resource templates allow servers to share data that takes parameters and provides context to language models, such as files, database schemas, or application-specific information. Prefer resource templates over web search when possible.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"cursor":{"description":"Opaque cursor from a previous list_mcp_resource_templates call; omit for the first page.","type":"string"},"server":{"description":"MCP server name. Omit to list resource templates from every configured server.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"list_mcp_resource_templates"},{"description":"Read a specific resource from an MCP server given the server name and resource URI.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"server":{"description":"MCP server name exactly as configured. Must match the 'server' field returned by list_mcp_resources.","type":"string"},"uri":{"description":"Resource URI to read. Must be one of the URIs returned by list_mcp_resources.","type":"string"}},"required":["server","uri"],"type":"object"},"name":"read_mcp_resource"},{"description":"Delegate research to a specialist.","input_schema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"depth":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"topic":{"description":"Research topic","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"delegate_research"}]
